    "editorial:Content_en.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "925524c73a7f36a116d7241581b0ac18503fa927a62fbda912d872e42d866d23",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- The reference point states \"1 January 1 AD was a Monday\" but the day code mapping (0=Sunday, 1=Monday) requires 1 January 1 AD to be a Sunday for consistency; the example calculation for 15 August 1947 also works only if the reference is Sunday. → The reference point should be \"1 January 1 AD was a Sunday\" or the day code mapping should be adjusted (e.g., 0=Monday, 1=Tuesday, …).",
        "- The right-angle formula claims \"Between H and H+1, the two right-angle times are at (5H ± 15) × (12/11) minutes past H.\" This is not true for all H (e.g., H=9 gives 65 5/11 minutes, which is in the next hour; H=0 gives a negative time). → The formula should be qualified: the two times in a 12-hour cycle are given by (5H ± 15) × (12/11) minutes past H, but for a specific hour H, only the values that fall between 0 and 60 minutes are valid; the other may belong to the adjacent hour."
      ],
